Our client is an international product-based IT company specializing in the iGaming industry. Born in 2014, they rocked the CIS region, and now take the success to the world. We are currently looking for a SEO specialist to drive organic growth in highly competitive niches, including iGaming and betting. This role is focused on strengthening online presence and supporting the overall growth of projects. 📋 Key responsibilities and your contribution:
Developing SEO strategies for cross-brand websites targeting;
Launching and reviewing websites: preparing technical requirements for developers and conducting technical audits of launched sites;
Managing website content: semantic core collection, keyword clustering, text analysis of competitors’ articles, preparing briefs for copywriters, generating texts with AI, and reviewing completed content;
Off-page optimization: auditing the backlink profile of the site and its competitors, preparing anchor lists, and purchasing links;
Searching for and selecting drop domains, participating in auctions and purchasing them, restoring domains, placing links, and sourcing new domains;
Monitoring search results and reacting quickly to changes;
Analyzing competitor strategies and identifying growth opportunities for promoted websites;
Monitoring and analytics, including conversion-focused work;
Testing hypotheses: running A/B tests, analyzing results, and adjusting approaches accordingly.

2+ years of hands-on SEO experience;
Proven experience in betting / iGaming / gambling, or other gray-area, highly competitive niches targeting the CIS market, with a solid understanding of the restrictions and specifics involved;
Ability to conduct competitor analysis and develop SEO strategies;
Strong expertise in technical SEO, content strategy, and link building;
Proficiency with the following tools: Ahrefs, SEMrush, GSC, GA4, Screaming Frog, Jira;
Working knowledge of CSS/HTML required for SEO tasks;
Ability to independently source and purchase drop domains;
Experience collaborating with developers and copywriters;
Self-sufficiency, strong organizational skills, and a willingness to grow and test hypotheses.
➕ Nice to have: Experience with behavioral factor manipulation is a strong plus.

Benefits: ⭐ Time Off & Recovery: 20 working days of fully paid annual leave, fully paid sick leave, and public holidays off according to company policy. ⭐ Health & Wellness: A flexible Benefits cafeteria that allows you to choose the perks that fit you best, with options including medical support, regular check-ups, mental health services, or gym access. ⭐ Education & Development: Internal and external training, industry events, language courses, and professional service subscriptions. ⭐ Workspace & Tech: All necessary corporate equipment provided, the flexibility to work fully remotely, and premium digital tools to enhance performance (e.g., AI tools, ChatGPT Plus). ⭐ Work Environment & Perks: Holiday bonuses, gifts for special occasions, paid business trips, and team events.

